# Go sources go through gofmt, which counts line endings: on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true `gofmt -l src/` lists every file in the directory (the working
# src/xswitcher.go carried 2138 CR characters while the index held CR=0), so the gate cannot tell a
# real formatting defect from a checkout artifact. Pinned to LF the same way the stand scripts are.
*.go text eol=lf
# The stand runs inside a Linux container: bash and python choke on CRLF.
stand/*.sh text eol=lf
stand/*.py text eol=lf
stand/Dockerfile text eol=lf
stand/*.c text eol=lf
# The build reads these two as data: apt-deps.txt is piped into xargs, so a stray CR would turn a
# package name into one apt cannot find, and Dockerfile.gui is parsed line by line. On a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true the working copy would otherwise arrive with CRLF.
stand/Dockerfile.gui text eol=lf
stand/apt-deps.txt text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
